{"name":"Fake Love","hex":"#cc77ee","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fake","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Not real; false, fraudulent.","Insincere"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something which is not genuine, or is presented fraudulently.","A move meant to deceive an opposing player, used for gaining advantage for example when dribbling an opponent."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fake"},{"term":"love","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deep caring for the existence of another.","Strong affection."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have a strong affection for (someone or something).","To need, thrive on."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/love"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fake Love (Drake song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Fake Love\" is a song by Canadian rapper Drake, released as the lead single from his 2017 mixtape, More Life. It was co-written by Drake with Starrah, Vinylz, and Frank Dukes, while the latter two handled the song's production. The song was released for digital download on October 29, 2016, through Young Money Entertainment and Cash Money Records."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fake_Love_(Drake_song)"},{"title":"Fake Love (BTS song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Fake Love\" is a song recorded in Korean and Japanese by South Korean band BTS. It was written by \"Hitman\" Bang, RM, and Pdogg, with Pdogg as producer. The Korean version was released through Big Hit Entertainment on May 18, 2018, as the lead single from the band's third album Love Yourself: Tear (2018). Columbia Records serviced the song to US contemporary hit radio on June 12, 2018, as a single in the country. A remix, titled \"Rocking Vibe\", was released on June 4, 2018, and appears on the band's third compilation album, Love Yourself: Answer (2018). The Japanese version of the song was released for digital download and streaming on October 16, 2018, by Universal Music Japan as a single album that included the remix and \"Airplane Pt. 2\", both also in Japanese. \"Fake Love\" is an emo hip hop, rap-rock and electropop song which relies on rock instrumentals. The lyrics talk about a love that was once believed to be destiny, but turned out to be fake at the end."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/84/Fake_Love_%28Rocking_Vibe_Mix%29_Cover_Art.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fake_Love_(BTS_song)"},{"title":"Love","blocks":[{"text":"Love encompasses a range of strong and positive emotional and mental states, from the most sublime virtue or good habit, the deepest interpersonal affection, to the simplest pleasure. An example of this range of meanings is that the love of a mother differs from the love of a spouse, which differs from the love for food. Most commonly, love refers to a feeling of strong attraction and emotional attachment."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/63/BTS_Fake_Love_Airplane_pt._2_single_cover.jpg/250px-BTS_Fake_Love_Airplane_pt._2_single_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/63/BTS_Fake_Love_Airplane_pt._2_single_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/63/BTS_Fake_Love_Airplane_pt._2_single_cover.jpg/250px-BTS_Fake_Love_Airplane_pt._2_single_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABTS_Fake_Love_Airplane_pt._2_single_cover.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/f0/BTS_-_Fake_Love_musc_video_screenshot.png/330px-BTS_-_Fake_Love_musc_video_screenshot.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https:/